{title: 505 - I Need the Prayers}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #505 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 505}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I need the prayers of those I love, While [G]trav'ling o'er life's rugged [C]way,
[C]That I may true and faithful be, And [G]live for Jesus every [C]day.
[C]I [F]want my friends to pray for [C]me, To bear my tempted soul a-bo[G]ve,
[C]And [F]intercede with God for [C]me; I [G]need the prayers of those I [C]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]I want [G]my friends to [C]pray for me,
[C]To bear [G]my tempted [C]soul above,
[C]And [F]intercede with [C]God [G]for me;
[C]I [F]need the [C]prayers [G]of those [C]I love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]I need [G]the prayers of [C]those I love,
[C]To help [G]me in [C]each trying hour,
[C]To [F]bear my [C]tempted sould [G]to Him,
[C]That [F]He may [C]keep [G]me by [C]His pow'r.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]I want [G]my friends to [C]pray for me,
[C]To hold [G]me up on [C]wing of faith,
[C]That [F]I may [C]walk the [G]narrow way,
[C]Kept [F]by [C]our [G]Father's [C]glorious grace.
{end_of_verse}
